        ;; The clipper. A triangle or quad that touched the frustum is rebuilt as a small linked polygon and
        ;; walked once per frustum plane.
        ;;
        ;; Each of the six planes owns a SHADOW-VU1-CLIP-STRIDE-quadword record whose first quadword holds two
        ;; vertex links in lanes x and y and, in lane z, the address of the two-instruction subroutine that
        ;; measures distance to that plane. The other six quadwords are two vertex slots three quadwords apart.
        ;; Installing the plane test as a code address means the walk is written once and dispatches with jalr.
        ;;
        ;; A vertex that survives all six planes is projected, textured, and appended to the clipper's own GIF
        ;; buffer; the surviving vertex count is patched into that buffer's primitive tag just before the kick.
        ;;
        ;; vi01, vi02, vi06, vi07 and vi08 keep physical names here. The two polygon walks below load the two
        ;; ends of an edge from vi07 and vi08 in opposite order, so one name for either would be wrong in one
        ;; of them.
